Subject: [PATCH] Add DMI support for the PCSpecialist / TongFang GM7MG7P

Adds one `uniwill_device_descriptor` and one `uniwill_dmi_table` row. No
existing descriptor, row, field or bit is touched, so every other board in the
table keeps exactly the behaviour it has today.

Base commit: 5a24248f6422a0b673a47cbfd65e19a98eb4c8a9
  ("Bump minimum supported kernel version to 7.2"), the rev
  linux/patches/BASE_COMMIT pins and the same rev the local nix build fetches.
  The blob this diff is against hashes to 7a2eeae, which is the same base
  index line linux/patches/uniwill-laptop-force_charge_limit.patch carries.

To apply:
    git fetch https://github.com/Wer-Wolf/uniwill-laptop 5a24248f6422a0b673a47cbfd65e19a98eb4c8a9
    git am linux/patches/gm7mg7p-dmi-entry/uniwill-acpi-dm-gm7mg7p.patch
  or, to check it without applying:
    git apply --check linux/patches/gm7mg7p-dmi-entry/uniwill-acpi-dm-gm7mg7p.patch

Every bit claimed here, and why this one rather than the other seven candidates,
is recorded row by row with its evidence in feature-map.csv beside this file;
the upstream PR body is PR_DESCRIPTION.md. The short version: each of the eight
is either graded `confirmed-*` in ec/annotations/registers.yaml, or confirmed
live by a documented test that the driver's own interface acts on. The seven not
claimed are excluded with a cited reason each, and nothing here is claimed on
the strength of a write the EC merely accepted.

diff --git a/uniwill-acpi.c b/uniwill-acpi.c
index 7a2eeae..816c846 100644
--- a/uniwill-acpi.c
+++ b/uniwill-acpi.c
@@ -2860,6 +2860,17 @@ static struct uniwill_device_descriptor x4sp4nal_descriptor __initdata = {
 	.kbd_led_max_brightness = 2,
 };
 
+static struct uniwill_device_descriptor gm7mg7p_descriptor __initdata = {
+	.features = UNIWILL_FEATURE_FN_LOCK |
+		    UNIWILL_FEATURE_SUPER_KEY |
+		    UNIWILL_FEATURE_BATTERY_CHARGE_MODES |
+		    UNIWILL_FEATURE_CPU_TEMP |
+		    UNIWILL_FEATURE_GPU_TEMP |
+		    UNIWILL_FEATURE_PRIMARY_FAN |
+		    UNIWILL_FEATURE_SECONDARY_FAN |
+		    UNIWILL_FEATURE_NVIDIA_CTGP_CONTROL,
+};
+
 static const struct dmi_system_id uniwill_dmi_table[] __initconst = {
 	{
 		.ident = "AiStone X4SP4NAL",
@@ -3316,6 +3327,14 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id uniwill_dmi_table[] __initconst = {
 		},
 		.driver_data = &tux_featureset_1_descriptor,
 	},
+	{
+		.ident = "PCSpecialist GM7MG7P",
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "PCSpecialist"),
+			DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "GM7MG7P"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = &gm7mg7p_descriptor,
+	},
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(dmi, uniwill_dmi_table);
